  "content": {
    "id": "p33-q12-response",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "12",
    "prompt": "A bag contains three dark and two milk chocolates. Without looking Anna randomly selects a chocolate and eats it. She repeats this process until she eats her first milk chocolate, after which she stops eating the chocolate. What is the expected number of chocolates that Anna will eat?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$2$ chocolates.",
      "worked": "Let $X$ be the number of chocolates eaten, including the first milk chocolate. The possible values are $1,2,3,4$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}P(X=1)&=\\frac25\\\\P(X=2)&=\\frac35\\times\\frac24=\\frac3{10}\\\\P(X=3)&=\\frac35\\times\\frac24\\times\\frac23=\\frac15\\\\P(X=4)&=\\frac35\\times\\frac24\\times\\frac13=\\frac1{10}.\\end{align*}$$\n\n$$\\begin{align*}E(X)&=1\\times\\frac25+2\\times\\frac3{10}+3\\times\\frac15+4\\times\\frac1{10}\\\\E(X)&=2.\\end{align*}$$\n\nAnna expects to eat $2$ chocolates.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 60
  },
